{"id": "EUVD-2026-86717", "enisaUuid": "cb0556c6-ca55-35d9-9db5-86194b1ea223", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Fix NULL-ptr-deref when showing a void BTF type\n\nbtf_modifier_show() resolves the modifier and then calls\nbtf_type_ops(t)->show() unconditionally. For the void type (type_id 0,\nBTF_KIND_UNKN) kind_ops[] has no entry, so ->show is NULL.\n\nA \"const void\" (a modifier resolving to void) cannot be a map key or\nvalue - map_check_btf() rejects it because void has no size - so the map\ndump path does not reach it. But bpf_snprintf_btf() takes a type_id\nstraight from the BPF program, and passing such a \"const void\" from the\nvmlinux BTF NULL-derefs:\n\nKASAN: null-ptr-deref in range [0x0000000000000028-0x000000000000002f]\nRIP: 0010:btf_modifier_show (kernel/bpf/btf.c:2914)\nCall Trace:\n <TASK>\n btf_type_show (kernel/bpf/btf.c:8251)\n btf_type_snprintf_show (kernel/bpf/btf.c:8321)\n bpf_snprintf_btf (kernel/trace/bpf_trace.c:1047)\n bpf_prog_test_run_raw_tp (net/bpf/test_run.c:829)\n __sys_bpf (kernel/bpf/syscall.c:4804)\n do_syscall_64 (arch/x86/entry/syscall_64.c:94)\n entry_SYSCALL_64_after_hwframe (arch/x86/entry/entry_64.S:121)\n </TASK>\n\nFall back to btf_df_show() when the resolved type has no show op; it\nemits the \"<unsupported kind:N>\" placeholder already used for kinds like\nFWD and FUNC. bpf_snprintf_btf() then returns the length as usual.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:24:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:13:14", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cf528f2d7a0a54f2a3c6d439cfa3c8d7dfe90d8d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/adb15557a641cb8a31f83e5f62bd12042b138c7b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/62b00074b58ccf43f61f70f2cfcac80937b530c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/86d86f9fcf62dd3654090fbf3cf7ae5f42aa0706", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/717abdfd1d559d01fdd102023f0a990fb0437240", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/98f1cb95221332139acf514350ae2cae3b8656c5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5324f4e75ff6e9c2ca2e267c5f34f0937f9d0ac9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4ea508b9ebd78bce7f212166d2e2cba66b875f08"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rf5p-p5fj-r25r", "CVE-2026-98064"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06b633ed-1682-3825-8952-220ff68c2922", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "0fa360b0-b34a-37ba-ba41-6dd8fbae6de9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "1634c43b-0883-3a24-a6f9-cfe134220efb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "1c50a3e4-4b86-3826-95af-e7325e4582b2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c4d0bfb45068d853a478b9067a95969b1886a30f <98f1cb95221332139acf514350ae2cae3b8656c5"}, {"id": "22a9f9c8-c1e0-356a-bcfa-175b7e4fcfee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "31cb9f70-4ebe-3023-be58-1bcfcf3dc51c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c4d0bfb45068d853a478b9067a95969b1886a30f <86d86f9fcf62dd3654090fbf3cf7ae5f42aa0706"}, {"id": "5b79ad8a-e2cc-3f2b-bfd8-51dd4b87b49d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "60264c9d-6fbe-39ff-a40b-1d08cc3ed463", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c4d0bfb45068d853a478b9067a95969b1886a30f <4ea508b9ebd78bce7f212166d2e2cba66b875f08"}, {"id": "69d0b396-3552-3638-8ca2-75c1e193408f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c4d0bfb45068d853a478b9067a95969b1886a30f <62b00074b58ccf43f61f70f2cfcac80937b530c6"}, {"id": "736b02d0-6565-3d49-8d78-2fc2d6192e12", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "73740a51-20